      "math_academy_id": "q-146193",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{6}, & \\,y=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}, & \\,y=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=4] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
